WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.940
So far, everything we have made
has lived in this one browser.

2
00:00:04.077 --> 00:00:08.538
This episode steps outside it: the gallery,
where people share what they make,

3
00:00:08.538 --> 00:00:12.277
and an account, which gives your
work a history in the cloud.

4
00:00:12.487 --> 00:00:15.387
Gallery, at the top, is open to everyone.

5
00:00:15.477 --> 00:00:17.287
No account, no sign in.

6
00:00:17.408 --> 00:00:20.596
It opens on a spotlight,
then rows: what's trending,

7
00:00:20.596 --> 00:00:23.728
what's new, and a row for
each kind of project.

8
00:00:23.939 --> 00:00:26.939
Search reads names, tags and descriptions.

9
00:00:26.989 --> 00:00:29.739
I'm after something for dinners, so: meal.

10
00:00:29.946 --> 00:00:33.906
Every project has a page: the
preview pages its author picked,

11
00:00:33.906 --> 00:00:35.816
who made it, and its tags.

12
00:00:35.875 --> 00:00:39.177
Download all variants gets
every PDF in one zip,

13
00:00:39.177 --> 00:00:43.485
and Version history opens any
version the author published.

14
00:00:43.691 --> 00:00:48.261
Open in editor copies the project
into your own editor, as a new tab.

15
00:00:48.408 --> 00:00:53.097
The copy is yours: change anything you
like, and the original never knows.

16
00:00:53.305 --> 00:00:56.585
Our recipe book, though, is
still only in this browser.

17
00:00:56.709 --> 00:01:01.730
On its tab, the Cloud menu has just one
thing to offer while we are signed out:

18
00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.569
Sign in to save to cloud.

19
00:01:03.883 --> 00:01:06.553
Sign Up turns the form
into Create Account.

20
00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:09.090
Your name and your email stay private.

21
00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:14.570
The username is public: it is the name the
gallery shows on everything you share.

22
00:01:14.776 --> 00:01:17.356
The password needs at
least twelve characters.

23
00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:21.810
Then Sign Up, and instead of signing
you in, it sends a link to your email.

24
00:01:22.016 --> 00:01:23.106
Here it is.

25
00:01:23.196 --> 00:01:27.596
Clicking the link confirms the address
and signs you in, all in one go.

26
00:01:27.803 --> 00:01:32.873
We're back in the editor, signed in, and
the Cloud menu now offers Save to cloud.

27
00:01:32.974 --> 00:01:35.754
Nothing is ever uploaded behind your back.

28
00:01:35.789 --> 00:01:40.583
Each save is a snapshot you choose to
make, with a message that says what it is.

29
00:01:41.068 --> 00:01:42.958
Let's change something we can see.

30
00:01:43.086 --> 00:01:46.836
Tomato Soup becomes Roasted
Tomato Soup, and we save again,

31
00:01:46.836 --> 00:01:48.866
with a message that says so.

32
00:01:48.946 --> 00:01:51.681
The message is for future
you: in a few months,

33
00:01:51.681 --> 00:01:55.596
Roast the tomatoes will still
mean something, and Update won't.

34
00:01:55.806 --> 00:01:58.956
Version history lists
every save, newest first.

35
00:01:59.005 --> 00:02:02.515
The top one is marked HEAD: the
latest version in the cloud.

36
00:02:02.722 --> 00:02:05.712
Restore puts an older
version back in the editor.

37
00:02:05.764 --> 00:02:09.619
It asks first, because anything
you had not saved would be lost.

38
00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:11.921
And there is plain Tomato Soup again.

39
00:02:12.145 --> 00:02:14.345
Restoring only changed this tab.

40
00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:19.002
The cloud still has both versions, and
saving now would simply add a third,

41
00:02:19.002 --> 00:02:22.397
so you can step back and
forth as often as you like.

42
00:02:22.611 --> 00:02:27.941
Everything the cloud holds for you is on
one page: My projects, in the account menu.

43
00:02:27.999 --> 00:02:33.063
Each project is private until you publish
it, and the bar on top is your storage:

44
00:02:33.063 --> 00:02:35.439
fifty megabytes for every account.

45
00:02:35.647 --> 00:02:38.753
Next time: publishing the
recipe book to the gallery,

46
00:02:38.753 --> 00:02:41.097
and what happens when somebody forks it.
